5. Remote services (optional, bring your own key)
======================================================================================================================

    Google Gemini (Live, Robotics-ER) and OpenAI-compatible LLM/TTS endpoints are called only with a key from
    .env or one a visitor enters in the browser. Their terms of service apply to that use.

    Photo -> 3D (pps/recon/providers, docs/RECON.md), only with a key the person brings:
      fal.ai, model fal-ai/trellis ... Microsoft TRELLIS, model weights and most code MIT (github.com/microsoft/TRELLIS);
                                       fal.ai's terms of service apply to the API use.
      Meshy image-to-3d .............. Meshy terms of use: outputs made on the free plan are owned by Meshy and licensed
                                       CC BY 4.0; on a paid plan the customer owns them; API outputs are deleted after
                                       3 days; no training of competing models on outputs.
    Opt-in, local (never downloaded unless PC_TRIPOSR=1):
      TripoSR (Tripo AI & Stability AI) MIT, code (github.com/VAST-AI-Research/TripoSR, not redistributed here) and
                                       weights (huggingface.co/stabilityai/TripoSR, 1.68 GB).
    Deliberately NOT offered (license limits): Tencent Hunyuan3D 2.x (its community license excludes the EU, the UK
    and South Korea and caps at 1 M monthly active users); Stability AI Stable Fast 3D / SPAR3D (Stability AI
    Community License, free only under US$1 M annual revenue); Depth Anything V2 Base / Large / Giant (CC BY-NC 4.0).

